  "scripts": {
    "project": "Narrated shape-only history short about the final 1803 campaign of the Haitian Revolution and the Battle of Vertières.",
    "sceneById": {
      "haiti-scene-1": "By November 1803, Haiti's revolution had reached a decisive final campaign. Jean-Jacques Dessalines led the revolutionary army against French forces commanded by General Rochambeau.",
      "haiti-scene-2": "On November 18, Haitian forces attacked the fortified French position at Vertières, near Cap-Français. Capois-la-Mort led repeated assaults under intense fire.",
      "haiti-scene-3": "A famous account says Capois kept advancing after his horse was struck down. The story helped make him a lasting symbol of courage in the Haitian Revolution.",
      "haiti-scene-4": "The French position collapsed, and Rochambeau soon agreed to evacuate. Weeks later, on January 1, 1804, Haiti declared independence and became the first independent Black republic."
    }
